INT. ABANDONED NURSERY SCHOOL, CLASSROOM - NIGHT

Tiny chairs. A rocking horse with no eyes. Peeling alphabet posters in the moonlight. A music box plays three notes and stops.

OFFICER DWIGHT MALLORY, forties, flashlight in hand, nudges open the door with his boot. His partner OFFICER SANDRA PELL, thirties, follows, gun low. A teenage urban explorer, TAYLOR REEVES, seventeen, trails behind with a camera, whispering. And at the back wall, so still she could be a coat on a hook, stands a girl in a yellow dress, MISS MARIGOLD, her face turned to the corner.

MALLORY
Police. Anyone in here?

PELL
Quiet. Listen.

TAYLOR
It's just the wind, right?

The music box plays again. Pell sweeps her light. Mallory crouches by the rocking horse and puts a hand on its empty socket. Taylor lifts the camera, the red light blinks, and the flashlight beam crosses the yellow dress.

PELL
Dwight.

MALLORY
I see her.

TAYLOR
Is that, is she a kid?

The girl turns. Her face is smooth and pale as a plate. She lifts one hand to her mouth, and the music box plays its three notes again.

MARIGOLD
(sweetly)
Nap time.
